From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Verm <183540171+vermingov@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:29:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] perf(linux): less memory and work at rest

- Fixed malloc thresholds: glibc raised its mmap threshold after the
  blocker's list compile freed large buffers, so the main process kept
  about 80 MB it no longer used (210 MB to 130-145 MB after a compile).
- Memory pressure from GLib's memory monitor (low-memory-monitor or the
  kernel's PSI): the warm spare view and tighter view limits now apply on
  Linux. A quiet minute after the last warning reads as normal.
- Extensions: the full sync runs once per profile, not for every new view
  (each re-sent every extension's scripts to every tab and re-added every
  network rule list); the plugin's data is built once per change; a
  popup's size follower is retired when its page reloads; the trace
  switch is read once.
- storage.set/remove skip unchanged values and serialize once.
